[Unit]
Description=Omarchy installation
Wants=omarchy-install-cpu-boost.service
# The umbrella for the install phases. The orchestrator starts
# it when an install begins; phase units (and the keyring init) declare
# PartOf= it, so `systemctl stop omarchy-install.target` is a group abort
# that takes every running phase's cgroup down with it. The ordering lives
# in the phase units themselves: each Requires= and After= its predecessor,
# and starting the terminal unit walks the whole chain.
#
# The destruction boundary: omarchy-install-disk.service partitions,
# formats and mounts the target, and every later phase unit runs strictly
# after it by those edges. run-phase enforces it independently — a hosted
# phase refuses to run unless the target is a mountpoint, so a stray start
# or a mis-edged graph fails loudly instead of writing into the live
# system.
